# kills: SAVE CHANGES is reachable without scrolling on a built-in-sized deck
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern SAVE.CHANGES.is.reachable.without.scrolling.on.a.built-in-sized tests/e2e.test.js
# The sheet body refuses to shrink, so it keeps its full content height inside
# a surface capped at 85dvh, the surface scrolls again and the footer under it
# is pushed past the cap: SAVE CHANGES starts 243px below the fold at 844x390.
# Note this is the "it fits on MY phone" defect - the eight-note Edit sheet
# clears 390x844 with a few pixels to spare and only fails in landscape.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
index 2681e9b..c861eb6 100644
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -139,7 +139,7 @@ button.nav:active{background:#2e281e}
    below its content and the footer is pushed out of the cap again.
    .sheetsurf keeps overflow-y:auto as the backstop for the degenerate case
    where the footer alone exceeds the cap. */
-.sheetbody{min-height:0; overflow-y:auto;
+.sheetbody{min-height:0; flex-shrink:0; overflow-y:auto;
   display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:9px}
 .sheetlabel{font:600 9.5px/1.5 "Nunito Sans"; letter-spacing:.13em; color:#a79d8b;
   text-transform:uppercase}
